1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,460
Nice job, boys!

2
00:00:12,820 --> 00:00:19,080
They were all so antsy during the opening ceremonies, but I don't think they look as nervous as they did during yesterday's practice.

3
00:00:19,420 --> 00:00:22,840
Right. Right. Okay, I got it. Thanks for that.

4
00:00:24,340 --> 00:00:25,280
Who was that, coach?

5
00:00:25,280 --> 00:00:25,540
Again!

6
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:28,660
Shimera from the Tokyo Metropolitan Gym.

7
00:00:28,660 --> 00:00:31,460
It seems the matches are moving faster than expected.

8
00:00:32,180 --> 00:00:35,700
It's really important to get warmed up properly, especially in the beginning.

9
00:00:37,080 --> 00:00:39,340
I was hoping we'd have more time to do that.

10
00:00:40,140 --> 00:00:44,140
It's about ten minutes to the Tokyo Metropolitan Gymnasium by bus.

11
00:00:45,160 --> 00:00:47,140
Hey, guys! Time to get going!

12
00:00:47,680 --> 00:00:47,960
Sir!

13
00:00:48,480 --> 00:00:48,820
Yeah!

14
00:00:52,540 --> 00:00:54,020
Mom, I have to go pee!

15
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:55,520
Well, hurry up and go!

16
00:00:55,520 --> 00:00:56,180
Mm-hmm.

17
00:00:56,180 --> 00:00:59,960
Oh, there, there. I know you're hungry.

18
00:00:59,960 --> 00:01:00,800
How long until the next bus?

19
00:01:01,180 --> 00:01:02,120
Four minutes.

20
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:03,440
Potty time!

21
00:01:03,880 --> 00:01:04,680
I'm gonna go, too.

22
00:01:05,200 --> 00:01:06,740
I can stay here and watch your stuff.

23
00:01:07,240 --> 00:01:07,800
Thank you.

24
00:01:08,080 --> 00:01:10,020
Thus foreshadowing missing the bus.

25
00:01:10,180 --> 00:01:11,420
Hey! Stop that!

26
00:01:12,620 --> 00:01:14,760
You first years have a lot of equipment.

27
00:01:15,480 --> 00:01:16,860
Can I help you carry some of it?

28
00:01:17,420 --> 00:01:18,480
No, no, that's okay.

29
00:01:18,480 --> 00:01:22,260
These nerves are gonna kill me if I don't keep busy with something.

30
00:01:23,580 --> 00:01:24,340
No problem.

31
00:01:24,340 --> 00:01:34,520
All right. Just stay calm.

32
00:01:34,720 --> 00:01:36,880
Daiichi, you do know you're talking to yourself, right?

33
00:01:37,040 --> 00:01:37,960
Shut up, man.

34
00:01:38,760 --> 00:01:40,600
Asahi, you forgot your access pass.

35
00:01:40,960 --> 00:01:42,340
Oh, sorry about that.

36
00:01:42,480 --> 00:01:45,440
Remember, they aren't going to let you in if you don't have this on you, okay?

37
00:01:45,440 --> 00:01:50,700
Everyone's still pretty stiff, but it's nothing I didn't expect.

38
00:01:51,420 --> 00:01:53,300
And now I need to calm down.

39
00:01:54,160 --> 00:01:54,680
Huh?

40
00:01:56,500 --> 00:01:58,200
What's wrong? Think you forgot something?

41
00:01:58,880 --> 00:02:00,320
No, it's this bag.

42
00:02:01,160 --> 00:02:04,160
It looks like mine, but it's not mine.

43
00:02:04,940 --> 00:02:05,140
Huh?

44
00:02:06,280 --> 00:02:07,440
Uh...

45
00:02:07,440 --> 00:02:10,980
My shoes were in it.

46
00:02:11,220 --> 00:02:11,840
They're gone!

47
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:11,900
They're gone!

48
00:02:11,900 --> 00:02:41,880
We'll be right back.

49
00:02:41,900 --> 00:03:11,880
We'll be right back.

50
00:03:11,900 --> 00:03:41,880
We'll be right back.

51
00:03:41,900 --> 00:04:11,880
We'll be right back.

52
00:04:11,880 --> 00:04:12,720
It's mine!

53
00:04:12,840 --> 00:04:14,120
Okay, calm down, you two.

54
00:04:15,140 --> 00:04:18,120
I'm just going to call the gym where we were doing our warm-ups.

55
00:04:18,620 --> 00:04:20,280
Should we go and buy some new ones?

56
00:04:20,420 --> 00:04:22,180
If it comes down to that, we'll have to.

57
00:04:22,280 --> 00:04:23,200
I'm so sorry!

58
00:04:23,760 --> 00:04:24,820
It's okay, guys.

59
00:04:24,920 --> 00:04:25,700
Nobody's dying.

60
00:04:27,300 --> 00:04:28,000
Hey, man.

61
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:29,280
Where's your phone?

62
00:04:29,280 --> 00:04:35,060
It's inside that bag!

63
00:04:35,260 --> 00:04:36,780
You're brilliant, Kageyama!

64
00:04:36,780 --> 00:04:37,420
Hello?

65
00:04:44,860 --> 00:04:47,640
Well, apparently no one over there has turned in a bag yet.

66
00:04:47,980 --> 00:04:50,860
I just found out that it was some kid that accidentally took it.

67
00:04:51,420 --> 00:04:53,160
His mom says they'll wait for us at the gym.

68
00:04:53,160 --> 00:04:55,220
Oh, thank goodness.

69
00:04:55,460 --> 00:04:56,440
It's still close.

70
00:04:56,760 --> 00:05:01,020
Yeah, but you forget that Shimura took the bus and went back home to pick up the crew from the neighborhood.

71
00:05:02,520 --> 00:05:03,220
I'll do it.

72
00:05:03,460 --> 00:05:04,620
I can go pick them up.

73
00:05:04,620 --> 00:05:08,140
I should probably be the one to go.

74
00:05:09,140 --> 00:05:09,960
It's fine.

75
00:05:10,120 --> 00:05:12,280
I have the speed and stamina to get there and back.

76
00:05:13,340 --> 00:05:15,280
Besides, I won't always be around.

77
00:05:15,680 --> 00:05:18,040
And I know you'll feel kind of lost without me next year.

78
00:05:19,260 --> 00:05:22,240
So now's the time for you to get started.

79
00:05:24,980 --> 00:05:25,420
Right.

80
00:05:25,420 --> 00:05:30,440
I promise he'll be back before the match starts.

81
00:05:31,080 --> 00:05:32,060
We're so sorry!

82
00:05:32,440 --> 00:05:35,480
This is probably too much, but try not to worry while I'm gone.

83
00:05:35,860 --> 00:05:36,480
Thanks, Kyoko.

84
00:05:36,780 --> 00:05:37,760
We're counting on you.

85
00:05:43,660 --> 00:05:46,600
Dear Kyoko, run like the beautiful and bouncy wind.

86
00:05:46,780 --> 00:05:50,020
It kind of makes me feel uncomfortable when you guys talk like that, so please don't.

87
00:05:50,280 --> 00:05:51,160
Come on, guys.

88
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:51,840
This is Kyoko.

89
00:05:52,040 --> 00:05:52,680
She'll be fine.

90
00:05:52,740 --> 00:05:53,060
Right.

91
00:05:53,220 --> 00:05:53,900
That's done.

92
00:05:53,900 --> 00:05:55,720
Let's concentrate on our match.

93
00:05:56,380 --> 00:05:58,380
We need to get down there and get warmed up.

94
00:05:58,860 --> 00:05:59,540
Yes, sir!

95
00:06:20,660 --> 00:06:23,560
After practicing and practicing and practicing,

96
00:06:23,900 --> 00:06:27,660
everything I had worked so hard for was over, just like that.

97
00:06:28,860 --> 00:06:30,640
What did I do differently at that time?

98
00:06:31,280 --> 00:06:35,100
I could feel my stride, my legs cutting through the air.

99
00:06:35,100 --> 00:06:39,580
But then, they hit something.

100
00:06:39,580 --> 00:06:40,980
Something hard.

101
00:06:40,980 --> 00:06:45,380
And my heart, it felt like it just stopped.

102
00:06:45,380 --> 00:06:53,220
Got this!

103
00:06:53,220 --> 00:06:54,220
One more lap!

104
00:07:01,900 --> 00:07:03,800
Kyoko, have you joined the club yet?

105
00:07:04,760 --> 00:07:07,300
I think you'd make a great volleyball manager.

106
00:07:07,300 --> 00:07:20,180
Maybe it was just that somehow the fact scared me, even more than I realized.

107
00:07:20,180 --> 00:07:21,900
Sure.

108
00:07:21,900 --> 00:07:31,020
The volleyball team hadn't had a manager for a long time, so I had to figure out a lot of

109
00:07:31,020 --> 00:07:31,720
it on my own.

110
00:07:32,380 --> 00:07:36,380
The rules of the game, the referee's hand signals, how points were scored.

111
00:07:36,380 --> 00:07:47,900
It felt good to devote myself to something, but part of me still felt like I was on the outside, and it was a relief to know that I wasn't out there on the front lines.

112
00:07:47,900 --> 00:07:57,460
But as time went on, gradually, the boys on the team stopped feeling like strangers to me.

113
00:08:01,460 --> 00:08:02,140
Listen up.

114
00:08:02,860 --> 00:08:05,180
The floors here will be much harder to slide on.

115
00:08:05,340 --> 00:08:07,280
They're not like the wooden floors you're all used to.

116
00:08:07,960 --> 00:08:10,320
If you dive at the floor like usual, you'll get hurt.

117
00:08:10,640 --> 00:08:12,420
Use your sweat to get rid of some friction.

118
00:08:13,020 --> 00:08:13,680
Yes, sir!

119
00:08:13,680 --> 00:08:18,080
Thank you very much!

120
00:08:18,860 --> 00:08:19,180
Right!

121
00:08:19,720 --> 00:08:20,200
Go!

122
00:08:20,700 --> 00:08:21,100
Yeah!

123
00:08:23,100 --> 00:08:26,580
That high ceiling's probably gonna cause more trouble than I bargained for.

124
00:08:26,960 --> 00:08:27,220
Huh?

125
00:08:28,420 --> 00:08:31,560
It's our first time playing in this arena, and it's enormous.

126
00:08:32,500 --> 00:08:37,000
We're just gonna have to accept that it's gonna take them some time to get a good feel for all that space.

127
00:08:38,780 --> 00:08:40,520
Hit the ball higher than usual!

128
00:08:41,200 --> 00:08:41,900
Yes, sir!

129
00:08:43,680 --> 00:08:46,520
It's so bright!

130
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:48,440
Ah!

131
00:08:48,960 --> 00:08:50,040
Come on!

132
00:08:50,240 --> 00:08:51,560
Gotta start paying attention!

133
00:08:51,880 --> 00:08:52,440
All right!

134
00:08:53,120 --> 00:08:53,720
Oh, man.

135
00:08:54,360 --> 00:08:58,320
It takes me forever to get my hands to warm up whenever I'm really nervous.

136
00:08:58,740 --> 00:09:00,280
Do you think you'll need some gloves?

137
00:09:00,540 --> 00:09:01,120
Uh, no.

138
00:09:01,180 --> 00:09:01,680
I'll be good.

139
00:09:02,460 --> 00:09:04,420
So don't you ever get nervous, Kageyama?

140
00:09:04,960 --> 00:09:05,580
I do.

141
00:09:06,320 --> 00:09:07,520
But not right now.

142
00:09:08,140 --> 00:09:08,960
Well, why not?

143
00:09:09,620 --> 00:09:11,940
This is just another step forward.

144
00:09:11,940 --> 00:09:14,460
Hey!

145
00:09:14,580 --> 00:09:15,720
It doesn't answer my question!

146
00:09:15,720 --> 00:09:16,720
Uh...

147
00:09:16,720 --> 00:09:27,320
Come on, shoes!

148
00:09:27,400 --> 00:09:28,280
Hurry up already!

149
00:09:28,280 --> 00:09:28,400
Okay!

150
00:09:28,400 --> 00:09:35,200
The team manager job.

151
00:09:35,200 --> 00:09:37,140
I just kind of took it on a whim.

152
00:09:42,140 --> 00:09:45,320
The position had been empty before I showed up.

153
00:09:45,320 --> 00:09:49,640
So I figured, once I left, it would just go back to how it was.

154
00:09:49,640 --> 00:09:52,640
But now...

155
00:09:52,640 --> 00:09:55,320
Now things are different.

156
00:09:55,320 --> 00:09:58,820
Now I need to pass the torch.

157
00:10:00,060 --> 00:10:02,320
There's someone else who's going to need it.

158
00:10:02,320 --> 00:10:15,840
After practicing, and practicing, and practicing, and practicing, everything you worked for ends so much faster than you ever expected.

159
00:10:15,840 --> 00:10:19,080
But so what?

160
00:10:20,740 --> 00:10:23,000
This doesn't mean I'm convinced we'll lose.

161
00:10:24,060 --> 00:10:26,120
This doesn't mean I'm convinced we'll win.

162
00:10:28,260 --> 00:10:30,340
I won't be standing on that court.

163
00:10:31,020 --> 00:10:32,780
I won't even be wearing the uniform.

164
00:10:33,880 --> 00:10:35,840
But right now...

165
00:10:35,840 --> 00:10:39,940
I have to take on this challenge.

166
00:10:48,640 --> 00:10:51,480
For me, right now...

167
00:10:51,480 --> 00:10:53,160
This is the front lines.

168
00:10:53,160 --> 00:10:56,400
I've got the shoes!

169
00:11:16,880 --> 00:11:18,220
You did it, Kyoko!

170
00:11:19,080 --> 00:11:20,040
I'm so sorry!

171
00:11:20,200 --> 00:11:20,840
I'm so sorry!

172
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:21,620
I'm so sorry!

173
00:11:21,620 --> 00:11:24,720
I think I can jump about five meters now!

174
00:11:24,980 --> 00:11:25,340
Oh?

175
00:11:25,480 --> 00:11:27,080
I cannot wait to see that.

176
00:11:27,940 --> 00:11:28,280
Hey!

177
00:11:28,900 --> 00:11:29,840
Line up, guys!

178
00:11:29,840 --> 00:11:30,440
We are...

179
00:11:30,440 --> 00:11:32,120
FUN!

180
00:11:33,020 --> 00:11:33,400
Yeah!

181
00:11:37,240 --> 00:11:39,260
My freaking nerves are about to kill me.

182
00:11:39,400 --> 00:11:41,800
So let's at least make sure that everyone can hear us out there.

183
00:11:42,040 --> 00:11:42,560
Come on.

184
00:11:42,600 --> 00:11:45,560
Don't make it sound like the only thing we know how to do is yell really loud.

185
00:11:51,620 --> 00:12:07,980
Ladies and gentlemen, we have Karasuno High School versus the squad of Tsubakihara Academy.

186
00:12:07,980 --> 00:12:09,720
Let the game begin!

187
00:12:10,480 --> 00:12:11,520
Let's play!

188
00:12:11,520 --> 00:12:16,520
Frankly, considering how nervous everyone was, I was pretty worried earlier.

189
00:12:16,840 --> 00:12:18,420
But they seem to have recovered nicely.

190
00:12:19,240 --> 00:12:20,740
Yeah, Hinata in particular.

191
00:12:21,180 --> 00:12:23,880
Maybe his losing his shoes was actually something of a blessing.

192
00:12:24,320 --> 00:12:26,800
We can thank Kyoko for making sure it wasn't a nightmare.

193
00:12:27,520 --> 00:12:27,960
Yeah!

194
00:12:27,960 --> 00:12:31,220
You doing okay, Maruyama?

195
00:12:31,820 --> 00:12:34,500
Looks to me like you have some bad performance anxiety.

196
00:12:34,840 --> 00:12:35,100
Uh-huh.

197
00:12:35,700 --> 00:12:36,440
I'm okay, sir.

198
00:12:36,720 --> 00:12:38,760
We were back home before I knew it last year.

199
00:12:39,100 --> 00:12:40,740
And I'm not repeating that nightmare again.

200
00:12:41,100 --> 00:12:44,020
Yeah, you were a total wreck last year at our first championship.

201
00:12:44,700 --> 00:12:45,940
Let's focus up here, boys.

202
00:12:46,440 --> 00:12:48,940
Remember to use your serves to divide up their attacks.

203
00:12:48,940 --> 00:12:52,020
If we don't give him a lot of places to send the ball, we can take them.

204
00:12:52,500 --> 00:12:54,600
But don't take your eyes off their number 10.

205
00:12:55,300 --> 00:12:57,620
He'll hit the ball from where we're least expecting it.

206
00:12:57,720 --> 00:12:58,340
Yes, sir!

207
00:13:00,920 --> 00:13:02,780
They're totally staring at us.

208
00:13:03,060 --> 00:13:06,400
That's the team that ended up knocking Shiratorizawa out last fall, isn't it?

209
00:13:06,540 --> 00:13:08,580
I'd say we just try not to think about that.

210
00:13:08,960 --> 00:13:11,820
And I'd say you'd rather be playing Shiratorizawa now?

211
00:13:12,160 --> 00:13:12,580
Uh-huh.

212
00:13:15,880 --> 00:13:16,940
Oh, hell no.

213
00:13:16,940 --> 00:13:17,420
Right.

214
00:13:18,540 --> 00:13:22,820
We watched their qualifiers game, and it's not like they were able to crush Shiratorizawa or anything.

215
00:13:23,360 --> 00:13:26,160
Always remember, there is such a thing as a lucky break.

216
00:13:27,220 --> 00:13:27,620
Hmm.

217
00:13:29,580 --> 00:13:30,060
Oh!

218
00:13:30,460 --> 00:13:32,500
We're lucky we're not playing Ushiwaka.

219
00:13:33,060 --> 00:13:33,540
Exactly.

220
00:13:35,960 --> 00:13:39,960
You always know how to push the young guys and take their thinking in a positive direction.

221
00:13:40,560 --> 00:13:41,240
Of course.

222
00:13:41,440 --> 00:13:44,480
It doesn't change the fact that those guys did beat Shiratorizawa.

223
00:13:44,480 --> 00:13:47,480
But that, that's not going to matter much anymore.

224
00:13:48,700 --> 00:13:52,000
Maru's not the only player on this team who regrets last year.

225
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:57,780
Every team here has defeated one powerhouse school or another to qualify.

226
00:13:58,560 --> 00:14:03,440
And these powerhouse beating powerhouses may still disappear in the blink of an eye.

227
00:14:04,180 --> 00:14:11,460
And in this first match, the team that gets swallowed up by their opponents, by the stadium, is the one that disappears.

228
00:14:14,020 --> 00:14:15,660
Hit him with a killer serve!

229
00:14:15,660 --> 00:14:24,420
That's out!

230
00:14:25,220 --> 00:14:26,300
Good eye!

231
00:14:27,160 --> 00:14:28,360
I'm sorry, everyone.

232
00:14:28,780 --> 00:14:29,340
It's fine.

233
00:14:29,460 --> 00:14:30,360
I'm going to get the next one.

234
00:14:30,360 --> 00:14:31,200
Smoky hide, do or die!

235
00:14:31,280 --> 00:14:33,080
Smoky hide, do or die!

236
00:14:33,180 --> 00:14:35,020
Smoky hide, do or die!

237
00:14:35,100 --> 00:14:37,020
Smoky hide, do or die!

238
00:14:37,020 --> 00:14:41,280
Sorry!

239
00:14:41,760 --> 00:14:42,180
Cover!

240
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:47,700
He deliberately served it right where the back row setter would have to cross somebody's path.

241
00:14:48,100 --> 00:14:50,860
He hit it to the worst possible spot like it was nothing.

242
00:14:51,380 --> 00:14:51,920
Taiji!

243
00:14:54,400 --> 00:14:55,240
Nice receive!

244
00:14:55,960 --> 00:14:59,120
One guy we have to look out for is number four, Tera Domari.

245
00:14:59,440 --> 00:15:03,560
He's 190 centimeters tall and can hit the ball even with a bad set.

246
00:15:03,560 --> 00:15:06,360
His attacks from the back row are pretty intense, too.

247
00:15:06,920 --> 00:15:10,580
So you do whatever you can to make sure he doesn't get over your block.

248
00:15:10,600 --> 00:15:11,220
It's yours!

249
00:15:16,260 --> 00:15:17,360
Chess! Cover!

250
00:15:17,540 --> 00:15:17,900
Tanaka!

251
00:15:19,760 --> 00:15:20,720
Too long.

252
00:15:23,320 --> 00:15:24,380
Nice kill!

253
00:15:25,240 --> 00:15:26,240
Sorry, guys.

254
00:15:26,520 --> 00:15:27,940
It's okay. Keep it going.

255
00:15:31,440 --> 00:15:32,220
Got it!

256
00:15:33,560 --> 00:15:35,160
Here he comes.

257
00:15:35,440 --> 00:15:36,040
Number 10.

258
00:15:44,040 --> 00:15:47,000
Chabaki high! Do or die! Chabaki high! Do or die! Chabaki high!

259
00:15:48,120 --> 00:15:51,480
In volleyball, the ball is almost constantly in the air.

260
00:15:52,660 --> 00:15:56,120
A sharp sense of spatial awareness is absolutely essential.

261
00:15:56,920 --> 00:15:58,580
But right now, they're nervous.

262
00:15:59,100 --> 00:16:00,840
And they've never played in this gym before.

263
00:16:00,840 --> 00:16:04,640
Those two factors are definitely throwing off that spatial awareness.

264
00:16:05,300 --> 00:16:09,060
And I suspect there's one thing that's been affected most by this new environment.

265
00:16:10,140 --> 00:16:13,660
The usually perfect precision of Kageyama's sets.

266
00:16:13,660 --> 00:16:27,540
I'll get there, but I'll need a little more time.

267
00:16:27,540 --> 00:16:29,260
Yeah, I know.

268
00:16:35,260 --> 00:16:36,800
It's too long.

269
00:16:36,800 --> 00:16:45,480
Kageyama's still adapting.

270
00:16:45,940 --> 00:16:47,900
We have to hold on until he figures it out.

271
00:16:48,400 --> 00:16:51,980
Well, Joe, you can definitely tell that Kurasuno High School is a bit stiff.

272
00:16:51,980 --> 00:16:55,360
Yes, it's rare to see Kageyama make such obvious mistakes.

273
00:16:56,240 --> 00:17:01,580
It's really hurting us that we weren't able to let Kageyama and Hinata practice together in this building.

274
00:17:06,080 --> 00:17:08,960
Teratomari drops the ball right into Kurasuno's midcourt.

275
00:17:09,080 --> 00:17:10,120
He's got a good eye.

276
00:17:10,120 --> 00:17:12,420
And with that, Tsubaki Hara pulls ahead.

277
00:17:12,440 --> 00:17:14,240
Kurasuno's setter is definitely off his game.

278
00:17:14,480 --> 00:17:14,980
Let's bait him.

279
00:17:15,440 --> 00:17:16,320
Their quick's not coming.

280
00:17:16,600 --> 00:17:17,740
Just keep to the left side.

281
00:17:19,480 --> 00:17:20,200
It's not?

282
00:17:20,660 --> 00:17:21,840
I thought it was next.

283
00:17:26,520 --> 00:17:27,180
Got it!

284
00:17:27,180 --> 00:17:43,180
Oh, yeah, guys, way to go!

285
00:17:43,300 --> 00:17:43,940
Keep it up!

286
00:17:44,300 --> 00:17:44,660
Damn it.

287
00:17:45,020 --> 00:17:46,160
He went for the left anyway.

288
00:17:46,720 --> 00:17:48,760
I tried to bait him, but they baited me instead.

289
00:17:51,080 --> 00:17:51,520
Okay.

290
00:17:52,180 --> 00:17:55,180
That one was about half a ball too short.

291
00:17:56,360 --> 00:17:56,760
Hmm.

292
00:17:57,180 --> 00:18:05,520
Too high.

293
00:18:10,580 --> 00:18:12,000
Damn these guys.

294
00:18:12,140 --> 00:18:13,360
They've got miracle shots now?

295
00:18:13,420 --> 00:18:14,040
We're fine.

296
00:18:14,220 --> 00:18:14,900
Freak accident.

297
00:18:15,060 --> 00:18:16,000
Let's just move on.

298
00:18:18,140 --> 00:18:19,460
What was that?

299
00:18:19,640 --> 00:18:20,600
It was awesome!

300
00:18:22,200 --> 00:18:23,640
I'm almost there.

301
00:18:23,640 --> 00:18:32,980
No matter how much you tell yourself it's okay and that you can catch up, the panic will

302
00:18:32,980 --> 00:18:33,800
still get to you.

303
00:18:33,800 --> 00:18:37,020
But if you let it swallow you, it's over.

304
00:18:37,020 --> 00:18:40,940
And that's why we're going to give them an early boost.

305
00:18:41,140 --> 00:18:42,140
Look at that.

306
00:18:42,140 --> 00:18:44,560
Yeah, he's throwing Tadashi in there pretty early today.

307
00:18:46,560 --> 00:18:50,680
In this tournament, I'm probably only going on the court to serve.

308
00:18:50,680 --> 00:18:56,020
That's why I've replayed this scenario hundreds of times in my head.

309
00:18:58,020 --> 00:18:58,900
Listen up, Tadashi.

310
00:18:58,900 --> 00:18:59,560
Tadashi.

311
00:18:59,560 --> 00:19:01,660
Don't wait for your nerves to settle on their own.

312
00:19:02,060 --> 00:19:03,820
You need to practice calming them yourself.

313
00:19:04,860 --> 00:19:08,140
And the most effective way for you to do that is finding a reset point.

314
00:19:08,240 --> 00:19:08,700
Uh-huh.

315
00:19:08,700 --> 00:19:13,920
The first thing to do, when you're warming up, look for a spot you can focus on.

316
00:19:14,660 --> 00:19:19,120
It can be anything that won't move, like a poster or a logo or the lights of an emergency

317
00:19:19,120 --> 00:19:19,540
exit.

318
00:19:20,180 --> 00:19:22,620
For now, we're just going to use that bag over there.

319
00:19:28,640 --> 00:19:30,140
First, I reset my emotions.

320
00:19:30,660 --> 00:19:31,580
Then I take aim.

321
00:19:33,860 --> 00:19:36,940
My target is the spot behind their ace.

322
00:19:38,700 --> 00:19:43,300
To hit it there, I have to send the ball over the right part of the net.

323
00:19:50,120 --> 00:19:51,900
It's going towards their libero.

324
00:19:54,280 --> 00:19:55,480
Damn, I hesitated.

325
00:19:55,720 --> 00:19:56,660
We threw him off.

326
00:19:57,160 --> 00:19:57,720
That's you go.

327
00:19:57,960 --> 00:19:58,420
Finish it.

328
00:19:58,900 --> 00:20:00,020
Three blockers.

329
00:20:02,920 --> 00:20:03,740
Nice one.

330
00:20:05,180 --> 00:20:06,580
First block of the day.

331
00:20:07,960 --> 00:20:08,520
Receivers.

332
00:20:08,700 --> 00:20:10,320
You need to make up your minds faster.

333
00:20:10,700 --> 00:20:11,240
Yes, sir.

334
00:20:13,180 --> 00:20:15,100
Tanashi, serve up a good one.

335
00:20:20,700 --> 00:20:21,100
Yeah!

336
00:20:24,700 --> 00:20:25,260
Yeah!

337
00:20:27,400 --> 00:20:28,980
Yes, yes, yes!

338
00:20:29,440 --> 00:20:31,400
How much did that kid improve?

339
00:20:31,580 --> 00:20:33,160
It hasn't even been that long.

340
00:20:33,160 --> 00:20:35,160
One more!

341
00:20:35,160 --> 00:20:35,660
One more!

342
00:20:38,980 --> 00:20:39,560
My go!

343
00:20:39,780 --> 00:20:40,260
Got it!

344
00:20:43,940 --> 00:20:46,320
Tsubakihara has just ended Karasuno's run.

345
00:20:46,820 --> 00:20:49,960
But it does look like Karasuno is finally gaining some momentum, Joe.

346
00:20:50,700 --> 00:20:53,320
All right, let's keep going into those double digits.

347
00:20:53,880 --> 00:20:54,360
Yeah!

348
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:56,520
Tsukishiba!

349
00:20:56,520 --> 00:20:59,600
Nice kill, Tsuki!

350
00:20:59,600 --> 00:20:59,740
Tsuki!

351
00:21:00,740 --> 00:21:01,140
Yes!

352
00:21:01,380 --> 00:21:02,380
Nice job out there!

353
00:21:02,460 --> 00:21:03,340
Keep it going, boys!

354
00:21:05,480 --> 00:21:08,640
But still, we can't seem to close the gap.

355
00:21:08,640 --> 00:21:16,920
Okay, I think I got it.

356
00:21:19,460 --> 00:21:20,020
To me.

357
00:21:20,240 --> 00:21:21,340
Come on, send it my way.

358
00:21:21,540 --> 00:21:21,980
Send it to me.

359
00:21:22,220 --> 00:21:22,600
Give it to me.

360
00:21:22,800 --> 00:21:23,120
Give it to me.

361
00:21:23,240 --> 00:21:23,680
I want it.

362
00:21:23,840 --> 00:21:24,120
Come on.

363
00:21:24,260 --> 00:21:24,680
Give it to me.

364
00:21:24,740 --> 00:21:25,020
Come on.

365
00:21:25,180 --> 00:21:25,360
Yeah!

366
00:21:25,360 --> 00:21:31,060
I bet if Hinata ever gets scared of messing up, he just pushes that feeling aside.

367
00:21:32,560 --> 00:21:35,140
And, well, it seems to be working.

368
00:21:35,140 --> 00:21:59,300
Boom.

369
00:22:01,300 --> 00:22:02,420
Perfection.

370
00:22:02,420 --> 00:22:14,860
I'm there.

371
00:22:15,860 --> 00:22:16,940
Sorry it took so long.

372
00:22:32,420 --> 00:23:00,140
Take it.

373
00:23:00,140 --> 00:23:30,120
Thank you.

374
00:23:30,140 --> 00:23:55,840
Next time, a chance to keep it going.

